**Episode:** *Thirty and One Hundred.* Lead is that a benchmark score has stopped being a property of a model. NVIDIA's AVO hit 100.00 RHAE on the ARC-AGI-3 public set running Claude Opus 5 (183/183 levels, 6,624 actions vs. VISTA's 7,542 with the same model) while ARC Prize measures Opus 5 alone at ~30% — NVIDIA itself says that's not a controlled ablation and is public-set-only, and the script says so. What survives the caveats is that AVO sent *zero image tokens* on a 64×64 text grid where VISTA renders a 512×512 PNG. DeepSeek shipped V4-Flash-Vision-Exp the same morning arguing the reverse; the buried tell is 27.3 on Agents' Last Exam beating flagship V4-Pro's 25.7 purely because text-only models don't see the multimodal items. Reconciliation is representational, not about scale. Third: Ox Alpha, anonymous on OpenRouter, 1M context, free, with dax's tokenizer fingerprint matching GLM-5.3 off by a constant 75-token wrapper.

